---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Terms | Credits That Count"
  description="The terms for using the free Credits That Count checker: what the tool is, its accuracy limits, acceptable use, and how to reach us."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section class="block" style="margin-top:26px;">
      <h2>Terms of use</h2>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: November 19, 2026</p>
      <p>
        These terms cover the use of Credits That Count and its free credit
        checker. By using this site, you agree to these terms. If you have
        a question about them, write to
        <a href="mailto:plans@creditsthatcount.com">plans@creditsthatcount.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>What the free tool is</h2>
      <p>
        Credits That Count is a free tool for students, their families, and
        counselors. It checks courses against the transfer information
        Louisiana colleges make public and shows, course by course, what
        the published record says about how a credit is likely to count at
        a target college. There is no account to create and nothing to buy
        on this site. Counselors may join the counselor list to hear about
        counselor tools; joining the list is free and creates no obligation
        on either side.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Accuracy and limits</h2>
      <p>
        Our results rest on publicly available catalog and equivalency
        data, currently the AY 2025-26 statewide common course catalog and
        the transfer sources published by Louisiana colleges. We report
        what those public sources say, and the checker names its sources.
      </p>
      <p>
        Colleges can change their requirements at any time, and the
        receiving college makes the final decision on whether a credit
        transfers and how it applies to a degree. Nothing on this site
        guarantees admission to any college, and nothing guarantees how a
        college will apply a credit. The checker is guidance for a family's
        or counselor's own decisions, prepared from the sources in effect
        when it is used. If you spot an error, please report it from the
        results page so we can check the source and correct the data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        The checker is for a family's own planning for its own student, or
        a counselor's planning with the students they serve. Please do not
        publish checker results as your own work, or use the checker to
        build a competing dataset.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="block">
      <h2>Questions about these terms</h2>
      <p>
        Write to
        <a href="mailto:plans@creditsthatcount.com">plans@creditsthatcount.com</a>
        with any question about these terms or about a result the checker
        gave you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="tagline-foot">Know before you go.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
